title: Value encoding in the store
tags: Storage [[Data model]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: How the store writes a value — a type byte once per field, then each value in a compact form of its type — the same everywhere a value is stored.

The store writes a value in one compact form, the same in a record, a pending write, a
pending index write and the log's before ([[Store tables]]). It changes only with a
conversion of the store ([[Persisted format changes]]). On the wire, and in what the
log endpoints show, a value keeps its column form ([[The column form of a value]]).

!! The parts

* ''varint'': an unsigned integer in LEB128 — seven bits a byte, the high bit set while more follow;
* ''zigzag varint'': a signed integer folded onto the unsigned ones (0, −1, 1, −2 …), then a varint;
* ''type'': one byte, the code of the value's type;
* ''uuid'': its 16 bytes, no length.

!! A value, by its type

The type is written once for a field, before its values: every value of a field has
the field's type ([[One value type per field name]]), and a field holding `nothing`
holds nothing else ([[Nothing versus unknown]]).

|!Type |!Value |
|`nothing` |— (the type alone) |
|`bool` |one byte, 0 or 1 |
|`int`, `datetime` |zigzag varint (a date in Unix ms) |
|`float` |8 bytes |
|`string` |varint length · its bytes |
|`ref`, `refbase` |uuid |
|`externalref` |the repository's uuid · the metarecord's uuid |
|`tree_ref`, `hierarchy_ref` |the parent's uuid (zero for a root) · varint length · the name's bytes |

A position's name is written once, as its exact bytes, which are its identity
([[Tree names]]): its displayed text is computed from them. A string is written as
bytes too, though the model holds only UTF-8 today.

!! A field, a record

```
field = varint len · name · type(nothing)
      | varint len · name · type · varint count · { value }
```

`tags = "foo"` is 12 bytes (1 + 5 + 1 + 1 + 4); ten tags 48. The column form that the
store wrote until November 2026 — the type as text and seven optional columns per
value, the field's name before each — took 32 and 320.

The extras a record carries while a pending write names it are written after its
fields ([[Mass writes in the store]]).
